<title>SRI LANKA: S.Lanka May foreign reserves down 11.5 pct.</title>
<headline>S.Lanka May foreign reserves down 11.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's Central Bank said on Tuesday the country's gross foreign exchange reserves stood at $1.72 billion at the end of May, down 11.5 percent from the end of December 1996.</p>
<p>In local currency terms, the reserves fell 8.1 percent to 100.89 billion rupees, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
